don't let the cute appearance of kenneth  bridges spirits deceive you combat in  this game is tougher than it looks  especially on its harder difficulties so  i'm here to give you a few general  strategies and tips as you progress  through the game to help you out and we  will be spoiler friendly if you enjoy  kena bridge of spirits subscribe to  gamespot to keep up with the latest in  gaming alright here we go  abuse your bow seriously once you get  the bow combat gets a little more  interesting its main use is to stun and  damage enemies by targeting their  courage weak points but keep in mind  that it's also good for farming bits of  courage over the fight as well every  little bit counts even if the damage is  minimal and yes there is a manual  slowdown ability that you can unlock  through your playthrough but also  shooting while jumping in the air  provides slow down as well without a  cooldown if you ever want to take a  couple second breather and survey the  surroundings on what to target next just  double jump and aim for a second to  strategize on what to do next  jumping is more powerful than you think  there are the standard defensive  abilities and can of bridge of spirits  pairing  shielding  and dodge rolling  but you'd be surprised on how many  attacks in the game can simply be jumped  over  this is actually the preferred method of  dodging attacks because you have the  ability to use the before mentioned  slowdown ability to counter attack while  dodging at the same time which none of  the other options have  here's a list of multiple useful things  you might not have known about in combat  shield sticks can be defeated with heavy  attacks but you can also defeat them by  shooting the small gap in its shield  the little explosive ticks can be  destroyed by simply pulsing them no need  to waste your arrows  small enemies can be disabled when a  bomb is thrown on them but also moths  are completely weighed down by an  attached bomb  and the best way to deal with multiple  pesky moths hands down is to bind  multi-shot an enemy then have the homing  shots do all the work for you and a  mage's magic bomb is parriable and can  be sent back towards them for good  damage  and talking about bombs your own bombs  while they won't damage you have the  ability to knock you off your feet which  can lead to an opening for an enemy  attack but if you learn the attack  sprint attack heavy you're able to  detonate the bomb and attack without  getting knocked back pretty nifty  parrying this is the biggest point of  contention parrying is all about knowing  what attack the enemy is going to do and  when the attack is going to hit you so  the biggest tip i can give is if you  don't know what the enemy is doing or is  going to do just don't try to parry it  this game has many attacks that are  delayed to purposely throw you off and  some that don't even look like attack  split can still damage you parrying in  this game has pretty strict timing and  failing to correctly parry will get you  killed quickly my suggestion is  obviously to learn the enemy patterns  first then bait them to do a specific  attack so you know when and where they  will strike that's the appropriate time  to parry take the wood knight for  example if you're at a distance 99 of  the time drawing your bow will cause  them to rush you down with the running  stab attack if you can bait them do that  and you know when it's coming parry away  or even purposely attack his defensive  stance shield to trigger his automatic  counter attack which you know is coming  so parry it right back  otherwise if you're going fresh into a  new boss fight with no understanding of  what their attack patterns are expecting  to parry no problem you might get one or  two off but you're probably going to die  and small side note if you're on ps5 or  pc set the game to performance mode or  60 frames per second parrying in 30  frames as with most action games is a  headache  pulse is useful as well not just  shielding while its main use is to  destroy corruption its other use is to  gather drops courage from a distance  without putting you in harm's way which  can be invaluable to top off that little  bit of extra courage you need to perform  your special rot attack  talking about courage like most games  this meter system can cap out which  means if you continue to attack while  you have full courage it's a complete  waste of hits you could be using to put  towards another meter of courage always  make sure you're being aggressive and  using courage as efficient as possible  but also maybe keep one held in the bank  in case of emergency if you need to heal  up  rot infused arrows and rod hammers look  pretty straightforward but have some  small quirks you might want to keep in  mind rod arrows are armor-piercing and  are definitely worth it when enemies are  lined up as they'll pierce through and  hit enemies that are standing together  more bang for your buck  rod hammers also do massive damage but  have two interesting traits they have  several invincibility frames during his  charge up which means you can't get hit  during the duration of this attack you  can use this to power through incoming  attacks also the rod hammer actually has  two parts the slam and the splash damage  doing this attack at close range right  at the tip of the staff will cause both  the slam and the splash damaged hit  doubling your damage  rod infused bombs are one of the most  useful techniques you'll get while  leveling up kenna but it slows down  enemies and incoming projectiles giving  you some breathing room to wail on your  opponent while it obviously uses one  courage bar when you use it its return  is higher than other techniques since  you have the ability to smack your  opponents around after they're stunned  so if you follow up quickly you can  usually gain back on average three  quarters of your current meter back they  just used up i'd say that's a pretty  good bargain deal to me  at last resort switch to story mode sure  if worse comes to worst your ego can  take a hit if you just want to enjoy the  game's story and progress further  there's nothing wrong with toning it  down for a fight that's just too  frustrating if anything you can tone it  down for just one battle you can't  handle then bring it back up after the  fight and for trophy hunters don't worry  about your first playthrough there's no  trophy tied to the difficulty settings  master spirit guide mode on the other  hand is another story you can't switch  difficulties on this mode so as the  saying goes suck it up buttercup you're  in for a tough ride now we'll go one  step further and leave you with an  advanced combat technique while it's not  particularly effective on smaller  enemies because jump attacks wiff  against them taller enemies and bosses  can be jump canceled against while it's  not overly powerful it does have the  ability to string together combinations  of attacks quickly to maximize your  damage done and courage gain during  counter-attacks  while you don't absolutely have to  remember everything here keeping at  least a couple of these in mind will  undoubtedly help you on your fights  through your journey with kenna and  remember we have more content as well  including the hardest difficulty  gameplay and a review of canada bridge  of spirits and for everything else  gaming keep it here on gamespot  oh  [Music]  [Music]  uh  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

